# Prairie Dog's "{4}{W}: Until end of turn, if you would put one or more +1/+1 counters on a creature you control, put that many plus
# one instead" (CR 614.1a, 122.6). On turn 1, with only three Moxen untapped after casting the Dog, it is refused (Mana: short);
# on turn 3 all five pay for it exactly and the pool is empty. Honor (a +1/+1 counter on target creature) then puts two on the Dog,
# a 4/4. The effect is gone on turn 5: a second Honor puts one, a 5/5.

